WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:05.720
After all these years and so many sequels,
it can be hard to remember what really happened

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:07.860
in all the Friday the 13th movies.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.020
Let's take a deep dive into Crystal Lake and
map out the entire gruesome story.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.800
What's the worst that can happen?

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:19.420
In the original Friday the 13th, audiences
first heard the sad, sinister story of young

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:20.620
Jason Voorhees.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:25.840
He drowned at Camp Crystal Lake in 1958, after
two counselors took their eyes off the boy

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.420
to go have some sexy-time.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:31.120
Those two counselors were murdered, and the
camp was subsequently shuttered.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:36.440
The camp reopens two decades later, but it
still has a reputation for murder and mayhem

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:37.880
— and rightly so.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:40.860
Meet Annie, freshly hired as a camp counselor.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:45.560
She hitchhikes to Crystal Lake, opting to
ignore the warnings of Crazy Ralph, a generic

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:48.699
townie who asks if she's going to "Camp Blood."

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:50.900
"You'll never come back again."

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.420
"Oh shut up Ralph."

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.100
"It's got a death curse!"

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:00.879
But maybe Crazy Ralph isn't so crazy after
all.

00:01:00.879 --> 00:01:05.360
Annie is chased through the woods by an unseen
assailant and brutally murdered… and she's

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:08.140
just one of several counselors to meet a grisly
end.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:11.940
It turns out Jason Voorhees isn't the killer
in the first installment.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:16.360
The murderer is his mom Pamela, who doesn't
want the camp reopened because of her son's

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:16.860
death.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:22.170
Twenty years of grief have curdled into madness,
and Mrs. Voorhees hears her son's voice urging

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:22.960
her to kill.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:28.400
Fortunately, an intrepid camp counselor named
Alice decapitates Pamela Voorhees, and that's

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.780
the end of this particular bad mama.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.780
At the end of the film, Alice has a nightmare
in which she's attacked by the rotting corpse

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:36.120
of young Jason Voorhees.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:39.200
It's surely one of the greatest jump-scares
of all time...

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:52.940
Alice swears it wasn't a dream…but police
say they never found a body.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.560
Strange, isn't it?

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:59.420
Friday the 13th Part 2 kicks off two months
after the events of the first film.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:03.560
We learn that Alice is still haunted by the
night she killed Pamela Voorhees.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:07.940
Little does she know that Jason is still alive
— and he's been living out in the woods.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:12.840
Jason tracks down Alice and totally kills
her… but not before stashing Mrs. Voorhees'

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:14.240
head in the fridge.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:18.680
As you might already know, Jason's trademark
hockey mask doesn't make an appearance until

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.600
the third installment of the franchise.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:24.900
Instead, we get Sackcloth Jason —- and here's
how that plays out:

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:27.040
"Sandra?"

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.700
This time, Jason is going after a whole bunch
of camp counselors in training.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:36.320
"It's great to have you all here at our new
counselor training center."

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:41.160
Clearly the legend of Jason Voorhees has grown
over the years — which we learn during a

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:44.640
bone-chilling exposition dump, courtesy of
head counselor Paul.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:46.980
"I'm going to give it to you straight about
Jason.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.520
His body was never recovered from the lake
after he drowned."

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:58.840
Jason does what he does best, using a variety
of weapons including a hammer, a spear, and

00:02:58.840 --> 00:02:59.520
a machete.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:04.760
He dispassionately stalks and murders camp
counselors… until only Ginny is left.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:09.740
She eventually finds Jason's shrine to his
mom, with her decapitated head front and center.

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:14.450
To elude Jason, Ginny pretends to be Pamela
Voorhees by putting on her old pullover and

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:15.660
stealing her hairstyle.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:18.000
He doesn't fall for it — because who would?

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:19.360
"It's all done, Jason.

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:22.880
You've done your job well.

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:23.660
Mommy is pleased."

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:28.200
After Ginny conquers Jason, she hobbles back
to her cabin to decompress.

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:32.000
She soon learns that a cute little dog named
Muffin survived the whole ordeal.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:37.020
Friday the 13th Part 3 is distinguished by
two major game-changers.

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:41.590
It's the first time Jason shows off his iconic
hockey mask, and it's the first entry in which

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:44.340
he isn't expressly terrorizing a campground.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:45.040
Meet Chris.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:49.640
Years before, she was attacked by a masked
figure in the woods near her home on Crystal

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:50.140
Lake.

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:54.880
Chris tries to confront her trauma by returning
to the scene, hoping it will help her to heal.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:59.020
She decides to bring a few friends along for
the ride... because why not make it a party?

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:01.240
"I shouldn't have come back here so soon."

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:03.320
"Don't let it get to you.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:03.820
Relax.

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:05.160
Enjoy the weekend."

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:10.280
Some of Chris' friends antagonize a bunch
of scary bikers, who retaliate by trying to

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:11.140
burn down her barn.

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:14.700
That's when we learn that a wounded Jason
had been hiding in there.

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:16.680
He immediately starts killing everyone.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:21.510
In their final confrontation, Jason reveals
his face to Chris — and it turns out he's

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:23.640
the one who stalked her all those years ago.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:26.400
She finally dispatches him with an axe to
the head.

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:32.340
And here's an interesting factoid for you:
The 1982 film was originally released in 3D

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:37.220
like several other horror sequels from the
era... including the awful Jaws 3D, and the

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:39.640
Satanic snoozefest Amityville 3D.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:43.240
Now we arrive at Friday the 13th: The Final
Chapter.

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:47.840
Following his apparent death in Friday the
13th Part 3, Jason is taken to the Higgins

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:51.160
Haven morgue... where he quickly proves he's
not quite dead.

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:54.360
He immediately kills a few staffers, just
to keep his hand in.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:59.200
Soon enough, Crystal Lake beckons, and Jason
— much like Lassie — makes his way back

00:04:59.200 --> 00:04:59.700
home.

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:04.880
Friday the 13th: The Final Chapter introduces
audiences to Tommy, played by Corey Feldman,

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:07.160
and his sister Trish, played by Kimberly Beck.

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:09.640
They're both visiting their Crystal Lake summer
home.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:13.370
They soon meet a rowdy group of high schoolers
hanging out in a neighboring house for the

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:13.980
weekend.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:19.000
Tommy is a quirky kid obsessed with creature
features, and he even makes his own monster

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.000
masks, as you can see.

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:24.620
Jason's killing spree inevitably brings him
to Tommy and Trish's house — and the quick-thinking

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:28.300
Tommy fights back using everything he knows
about Jason Voorhees.

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:32.460
He shaves his head and covers his face with
white powder, trying to remind the masked

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:34.520
killer of himself at a young age.

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:37.840
"Remember me, Jason?

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.180
Jason, don't you remember?"

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:46.820
This gives Trish a chance to use Jason's machete
against him… and his mask falls off to reveal

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:48.840
his increasingly monstrous face.

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:57.360
In the end, Jason is seemingly killed, and
Tommy looks into the camera with an expression

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:59.520
that suggests he might never recover.

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:02.900
Meanwhile, the Friday the 13th franchise bounced
back soon enough.

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:08.680
In Friday the 13th: A New Beginning, we learn
that Tommy Jarvis was indeed psychologically

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:10.560
scarred by his encounter with Jason.

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:14.000
As you can see, the experience has totally
changed him.

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:17.620
In fact, the character is played by a different
actor: John Shepard.

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:22.199
Five years after the events of Friday the
13th: The Final Chapter, Tommy still suffers

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:27.060
from severe post-traumatic stress, experiencing
flashbacks and extreme anxiety.

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:36.820
As you can see, he's quite the disturbed young
man:

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:39.460
"Yo man!"

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:50.900
Travis is admitted into a rural treatment
facility… one that's literally full of farm

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:51.400
animals.

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:55.240
The staff at Pinehurst Halfway House hopes
to help the young man get a better handle

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:56.020
on his past.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:07:00.340
And as you can see, this is a rare sort of
treatment facility that lets patients keep

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:01.479
sharps at the ready.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:06.500
Case in point: On Tommy's first day, patients
Vic and Joey get into a deadly disagreement...

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:10.820
"... um, to be perfectly honest with you,
I never really chopped wood before, but it

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:15.260
certainly looks like fun—" "LEAVE ME ALONE!!"

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:19.400
Before you know it, Vic murders poor Joey
with his trusty axe.

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:20.860
Paramedics rush to the scene.

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:23.139
"Is there someone we should notify?"

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:27.000
"As far as I know, there's no immediate family."

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:32.840
Suddenly employees and patients are getting
killed by a maniac in a hockey mask — and

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:34.480
everyone thinks Jason is back.

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:36.180
But something here doesn't add up.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:40.660
For one thing, the killer's hockey mask has
blue stripes instead of Jason's signature

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:41.160
red.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.980
Could this be a clue that the killer isn't
who he appears to be?

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:46.020
Could troubled Tommy be the culprit?

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:50.240
We eventually learn that Roy — one of the
paramedics that collected poor Joey's corpse

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:51.840
— was secretly the boy's father.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:56.880
Turns out Roy had a psychotic break after
his son's death and decided to become a professional

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:58.020
copycat killer.

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:00.240
"Roy was a real loner.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:03.220
Never talked much.

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:06.300
Not even to the other paramedics…"

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:10.920
Well, Tommy Jarvis just couldn't leave well
enough alone.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:15.580
At the start of Friday the 13th Part VI: Jason
Lives, the troubled young man takes a close

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:17.420
friend to Jason's grave in Crystal Lake.

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:22.200
Notice that Tommy is once again played by
a different actor — Thom Matthews this time.

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:26.900
Once they find the grave, they dig it up and
shove a metal rod into Jason's rotting corpse.

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:30.920
That's when lightning suddenly strikes the
rod, instantly reviving Jason.

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:34.740
The undead killer attacks Tommy and kills
his up-for-anything friend.

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:36.980
Tommy narrowly escapes with his life.

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:41.220
Of course, the police don't believe Tommy's
story because of his past mental health issues.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.220
"No, wait, you gotta listen to me!

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:45.320
Jason's coming and he's after me!"

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:49.779
The sheriff's daughter Megan is the only one
who believes Tommy, and she decides to help

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:50.280
him out.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:54.520
Jason quickly makes it back to the place where
he originally died… and plenty of children

00:08:54.520 --> 00:08:56.180
are already there for summer camp.

00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:00.580
Jason scares the kids, but for some reason,
he doesn't actually hurt any of them.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:05.640
Meanwhile, he gleefuly kills every adult and
teenager within a five-mile radius.

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:09.260
Thankfully, Tommy eventually wraps Jason in
some chains and drowns him.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:10.400
Or does he?

00:09:11.060 --> 00:09:15.900
In Friday the 13th Part VII: The New Blood,
we're introduced to the talented Tina Shepard.

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:20.679
She's your average American girl with telekinesis
— and we learn that she accidentally killed

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:22.800
her father by drowning him in Crystal Lake.

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:26.180
Tina is understandably traumatized by the
death of her father.

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:30.610
Many years later, Tina's sketchy therapist
Dr. Crews pressures her into returning to

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:33.760
Crystal Lake to confront her fears… or so
he says.

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:38.420
What he's really trying to do is understand
the scope of Tina's powers by using Crystal

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:39.420
Lake as a trigger.

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:43.400
She feels tremendous grief when she stands
in the spot where her father drowned… and

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:45.920
she also senses a dark presence.

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:49.980
It's Jason, and he finally manages to break
free from his chains.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:52.280
Needless to say, the killings begin again...

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:56.560
Meanwhile, a bunch of teens are preparing
for the world's wackest birthday party.

00:09:56.579 --> 00:10:00.429
"Party hasn't even started yet, and already
this place looks like closing time at the

00:10:00.429 --> 00:10:00.920
Stock Exchange."

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:04.640
"Russ, honey, we'll clean it up, I promise."

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:05.960
"Yeah, chill out."

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:10.500
Tina starts getting cozy with hunky Nick,
and Jason basically kills everyone.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:15.500
In the film's finale, Tina has an epic showdown
with Jason — with her telekinetic powers

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:16.739
on full display.

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:19.100
Look, she can even move couches with her mind.

00:10:19.589 --> 00:10:23.259
She unmasks Jason and discovers that he's
really let himself go.

00:10:23.259 --> 00:10:27.709
Oh, and then the ghost of Tina's father helps
chain Jason to the bottom of the lake... since

00:10:27.709 --> 00:10:29.540
that worked so well the last time.

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:31.600
Tina and Nick both survive.

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:32.800
"Where's Jason?"

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:34.900
"We took care of him."

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:40.060
Important note: The New Blood is the film
that features the notorious sleeping bag murder.

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:42.620
And then… this happened.

00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:47.160
The first half of Friday the 13th Part VIII:
Jason Takes Manhattan takes place on a cruise

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:51.839
ship — and we watch proudly as Crystal Lake's
graduating seniors embark on a class trip

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:52.820
to the Big Apple.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:57.180
Little do they know that the anchor of another
boat has come into contact with some ominous

00:10:57.180 --> 00:10:58.540
underwater wires.

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:03.140
An electrical current zaps Jason's chains
and reanimates him again.

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:07.020
He eventually climbs aboard the cruise ship
in broad daylight and starts killing a bunch

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:08.800
of recent high school graduates.

00:11:09.009 --> 00:11:14.060
To escape all the unthinkable horror, a handful
of survivors take a raft to Manhattan's shore…

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:16.400
but they fail to realize that Jason has followed
them.

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:18.780
And how does he fare in the big city?

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:20.040
Pretty well, actually.

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:27.800
"Yo man, It's cool man, you're cool."

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:34.960
In the end, final girl Rennie faces off with
Jason deep within the New York sewer system...

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:38.660
and she eventually gets her hands on some
extremely toxic waste.

00:11:48.380 --> 00:11:52.720
The film ends with Jason getting hammered
by even more toxic gunk, which presumably

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:53.360
kills him.

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:57.940
In the final scene, Rennie enjoys New York
with her boyfriend Sean and cute little dog

00:11:57.940 --> 00:11:58.440
Toby.

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:03.580
Jason Goes to Hell: The Final Friday isn't
the final entry in the series… but it's

00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:05.619
quite possibly the weirdest.

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:10.500
The trouble begins when the FBI intercepts
Jason on his way back to Crystal Lake, killing

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:11.840
him for the millionth time.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:17.140
Things get especially complicated when a medical
examiner decides to take a bite out of Jason's

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:18.200
still-beating heart.

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:23.400
Soon enough, some sort of Spirit Jason starts
taking over people's bodies... and all hell

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:24.320
breaks loose.

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:35.180
Jason Goes to Hell introduces some new supernatural
elements to the franchise.

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:40.020
For instance, we learn that only a member
of Jason's bloodline can kill him, and only

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:41.980
if they're armed with a special dagger.

00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:47.260
Jason's half-niece Jessica soon rises to the
task — and stabs Jason with the magic blade.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:52.500
In the end, Jason's mask is all that remains…
until Freddy Krueger's claws emerge from the

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:54.580
ground to drag the mask down to hell.

00:12:54.740 --> 00:12:58.060
Meanwhile, the Friday the 13th franchise remained
up here on Earth.

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:03.620
Much like the rest of us, Jason X tries to
pretend Jason Goes to Hell never happened.

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:08.350
The 2001 film takes place in deep space and
many years into the future.

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:12.780
The planet Earth has been ravaged by overpopulation,
war, and climate change.

00:13:12.820 --> 00:13:17.840
Scientists from the artlessly named Earth
2 are on a field trip to take samples.

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:22.720
They soon discover the cryogenically frozen
Jason inside the Crystal Lake Research Facility

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:26.200
— and they decide it's a great idea to bring
his body onto their ship.

00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:31.700
Jason soon thaws out, jumpstarting a highly
convoluted plot that draws heavily from Alien

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:33.140
and the Terminator series.

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:37.680
He obligatorily kills almost every member
of the crew, at one point even battling an

00:13:37.700 --> 00:13:39.760
android named KM 15.

00:13:40.049 --> 00:13:44.820
She wounds and almost kills Jason — but
as usual, he just won't die.

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:46.100
"You gotta be kidding me."

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:53.280
Freddy vs. Jason was an epic monster mashup
that combined two competing franchises.

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:57.550
The story finds A Nightmare on Elm Street's
Freddy Krueger in quite a pickle: He's lost

00:13:57.550 --> 00:14:01.299
a great deal of his power... because Springwood
residents just aren't afraid of him like they

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:01.880
used to be.

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:06.000
"Not strong enough yet."

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:09.320
So he hatches the perfect plan.

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:13.560
Back in Hell, Freddy poses as Pamela Voorhees
and awakens Jason.

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:22.400
"You are like a big stupid dog who can't stop
eating… even though your master said you

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:23.520
had enough!"

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:27.940
Jason is supposed to remind the people of
Springwood that Freddy is still a force to

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:31.200
be reckoned with — go ahead and call it
the ultimate PR nightmare.

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:35.540
"No..."

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:43.780
But things don't go as planned: Jason winds
up simply killing his prey instead of luring

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:44.620
them to Freddy.

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:49.080
The teenagers at the center of the story come
up with a confusing plan of their own: They

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:54.579
want to drag Freddy out of hell and back into
reality so Jason can definitively kill him.

00:14:54.579 --> 00:14:59.319
The final confrontation finds Freddy loading
up on one-liners while Jason maintains his

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:00.820
silent, singular focus.

00:15:01.149 --> 00:15:06.120
In the end, Freddy gets decapitated by Jason...
but his severed head later gives the audience

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:06.680
a wink.

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:08.320
What a coy little minx.

00:15:09.100 --> 00:15:13.400
The 2009 Friday the 13th reboot tried to bring
the franchise back from the dead.

00:15:13.540 --> 00:15:18.240
Once again, young Jason witnesses his mom
get decapitated by a desperate camp counselor.

00:15:18.260 --> 00:15:22.460
Decades later, a group of youngsters head
to Crystal Lake to search for an illegal pot

00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:22.960
farm.

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:26.320
Jason stalks and kills them all — except
for young Whitney.

00:15:26.340 --> 00:15:30.020
He kidnaps her because he thinks she looks
a lot like his dear dead mom.

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:34.389
Six weeks later, Whitney's brother Clay is
still looking for his missing sister.

00:15:34.389 --> 00:15:39.130
He goes door to door and eventually finds
Jason, who's been busy racking up more victims.

00:15:39.130 --> 00:15:43.140
Clay ultimately frees his sister and they
team up to kill the sick jerk once and for

00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:43.640
all.

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:56.200
Clay dumps Jason's body into the lake, but
at the very last minute, the unstoppable maniac

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:57.860
jumps up and grabs Whitney.

00:15:57.980 --> 00:16:02.240
Despite the cliffhanger ending, this is the
last we've seen of Jason on the silver screen.

00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:03.660
For now, anyway...

